<!--
  Road 1 is the parabola v = 0.01 * u^2 for u in [0, 40], as a <poly3> at the
  origin with hdg 0. Its @length is the closed-form arc length of that parabola,
    L = (u/2) * sqrt(1 + 4c^2 u^2) + asinh(2cu) / (4c) = 43.929203350866665,
  so its end is at (u, v) = (40, 16) with heading atan(2cu) = atan(0.8).
  The expected positions come from this formula, not from the numerical method
  in utils, so the test checks that method rather than restating it. u is not
  arc length: evaluating u = s would put the end 3.929 m too far along u.

  Road 2 starts 1 cm off that end, at x=40.01. Expected: 2 issues, one for
  each side of the connection (/OpenDRIVE/road[1] and /OpenDRIVE/road[2]).
-->
